      },
      {
        "type": "editor preferred term",
        "value": "elucidation"
      },
      {
        "type": "elucidation",
        "value": "Primitive terms in a highest-level ontology such as BFO are terms which are so basic to our understanding of reality that there is no way of defining them in a non-circular fashion. For these, therefore, we can provide only elucidations, supplemented by examples and by axioms"
      },
      {
